1
00:00:12,780 --> 00:00:14,680
Put this in...

2
00:00:16,260 --> 00:00:19,140
It's already this late? I have to hurry.

3
00:00:19,140 --> 00:00:21,240
At a time like this...

4
00:00:22,220 --> 00:00:22,620
Yes.

5
00:00:22,620 --> 00:00:24,540
Hello there, Reiko-chan.

6
00:00:24,540 --> 00:00:27,260
Dad, I'm sorry, but right now...

7
00:00:27,260 --> 00:00:30,060
Reiko-chan, what about that promise we made?

8
00:00:30,560 --> 00:00:31,360
Promise?

9
00:00:31,740 --> 00:00:34,220
The promise that you'd
get married this year.

10
00:00:34,220 --> 00:00:35,120
Married?

11
00:00:35,760 --> 00:00:37,860
You said so yourself at the
New Year's party this year.

12
00:00:37,860 --> 00:00:39,340
Did I?

13
00:00:39,340 --> 00:00:42,400
You did, you did.
The year's almost over, you know.

14
00:00:42,820 --> 00:00:45,740
Sorry, Dad, I don't have time right now.

15
00:00:45,740 --> 00:00:48,560
I'm about to miss my flight,
so I'm hanging up.

16
00:00:48,560 --> 00:00:51,540
Wait! I'm nearby. Look outside.

17
00:00:58,820 --> 00:01:01,620
Ta-da! I've missed you, Reiko-chan!

18
00:01:01,620 --> 00:01:02,420
Papa.

19
00:01:03,180 --> 00:01:04,640
I'm coming over right now.

20
00:01:07,580 --> 00:01:08,800
Whoops!

21
00:01:14,860 --> 00:01:21,040
Reiko-chan, you can afford an
apartment every season, after all.

22
00:01:21,040 --> 00:01:22,040
I searched high and low for you.

23
00:01:22,860 --> 00:01:24,160
Papa, really.

24
00:01:30,700 --> 00:01:33,020
Maybe I'll get married this year.

25
00:01:34,640 --> 00:01:36,520
And I have proof, just look.

26
00:01:36,520 --> 00:01:37,720
When did that happen?

27
00:01:38,220 --> 00:01:40,860
So, have you found someone?

28
00:01:41,440 --> 00:01:45,180
I have a few boyfriends,
but when it comes to marriage...

29
00:01:46,300 --> 00:01:50,380
Anticipating that, Papa went and
found some top-notch candidates.

30
00:01:51,980 --> 00:01:54,500
Don't tell me these are all omiai photos?

31
00:01:55,340 --> 00:02:00,260
I can't wait to see the face of the son-in-law
who will entrust the future of our Akimoto Group.

32
00:02:00,260 --> 00:02:01,960
Well, take a look.

33
00:02:04,800 --> 00:02:07,880
They're all spoiled sons of
the world's richest tycoons.

34
00:02:08,960 --> 00:02:11,240
Even Kei-chan's photo is in there!

35
00:02:11,680 --> 00:02:14,060
If we could become related
to the Nakagawa Konzern,

36
00:02:14,480 --> 00:02:17,300
the Akimoto Group would be like giving an ogre a club,
you know.

37
00:02:17,860 --> 00:02:19,360
This isn't the Sengoku period, you know.

38
00:02:19,360 --> 00:02:21,800
I refuse that kind of political marriage.

39
00:02:22,280 --> 00:02:23,040
Reiko-chan.

40
00:02:24,120 --> 00:02:26,580
So what kind of man do you want to marry?

41
00:02:27,240 --> 00:02:30,740
Family background or being
wealthy doesn't matter at all.

42
00:02:30,740 --> 00:02:34,760
I want someone strong and kind
who truly loves me from the heart.

43
00:02:35,320 --> 00:02:38,340
So if such a man appears, you'll marry him?

44
00:02:38,860 --> 00:02:41,200
If one appears,
I suppose I'd think about it.

45
00:02:44,420 --> 00:02:47,520
Because of you, Dad,
I'm going to completely miss my flight!

46
00:02:48,540 --> 00:02:51,740
Right, Dad,
take me to Narita in your helicopter!

47
00:02:52,780 --> 00:02:53,580
Hey.

48
00:02:54,880 --> 00:02:56,120
Okay, okay.

49
00:03:04,100 --> 00:03:06,000
Aren't you Reiko?

50
00:03:07,600 --> 00:03:08,700
Well, if it isn't Kei-chan.

51
00:03:09,280 --> 00:03:12,060
I heard you were skiing at
the Matterhorn over New Year's.

52
00:03:12,060 --> 00:03:14,160
I never expected us to
be on the same flight.

53
00:03:14,720 --> 00:03:16,060
What a coincidence.

54
00:03:16,640 --> 00:03:19,560
You're headed to southern France and Italy,
right, Reiko?

55
00:03:20,160 --> 00:03:21,600
Yes, as long as Kei-chan is with me,

56
00:03:21,600 --> 00:03:24,260
I guess I won't be bored even on the plane.

57
00:03:31,360 --> 00:03:33,860
Well, someone from the company
is here to pick us up, so

58
00:03:33,860 --> 00:03:36,260
Thanks. Have a great holiday.

59
00:03:36,260 --> 00:03:37,500
You too, Reiko.

60
00:03:40,460 --> 00:03:41,980
W-what's this? Who are you people?

61
00:03:44,280 --> 00:03:45,300
Ken-chan

62
00:04:14,120 --> 00:04:17,060
What are you slacking off for?
Get to work, get to work!

63
00:04:17,060 --> 00:04:19,640
At this damn busy year-end time!

64
00:04:19,640 --> 00:04:23,200
Nakagawa and Reiko are on
a long vacation in Europe.

65
00:04:23,200 --> 00:04:26,800
That's ridiculous.
I can't possibly work like this.

66
00:04:26,800 --> 00:04:31,100
You idiot! Those two took their
paid leave properly and are resting.

67
00:04:31,100 --> 00:04:34,580
Unlike you, who uses up all your
paid leave at the start of the year.

68
00:04:34,580 --> 00:04:37,760
Snuggling up to a stove like that...

69
00:04:38,900 --> 00:04:39,560
Get to work!

70
00:04:39,560 --> 00:04:40,660
Gurchi!

71
00:04:41,740 --> 00:04:42,680
Big trouble!

72
00:04:42,680 --> 00:04:42,980
What is it?

73
00:04:44,060 --> 00:04:45,520
Reiko's been kidnapped!

74
00:04:45,880 --> 00:04:46,240
What?

75
00:04:47,760 --> 00:04:50,240
Suddenly surrounded by a
group of men all in black

76
00:04:50,240 --> 00:04:52,440
I was struck on the head from behind.

77
00:04:52,440 --> 00:04:54,740
Then do you have any idea
who the culprit might be?

78
00:04:55,120 --> 00:04:56,480
No, nothing.

79
00:04:56,480 --> 00:04:59,600
Reiko got kidnapped while
you were right there with her?

80
00:04:59,600 --> 00:05:01,920
What was Nakagawa doing?

81
00:05:01,920 --> 00:05:02,840
Ryotsu

82
00:05:02,840 --> 00:05:05,380
Nakagawa got hurt too, you know.

83
00:05:05,380 --> 00:05:07,280
It's too harsh to blame him.

84
00:05:07,280 --> 00:05:09,040
I hope Reiko's all right.

85
00:05:09,040 --> 00:05:10,460
She's safe, right?

86
00:05:11,260 --> 00:05:12,140
Next,

87
00:05:14,060 --> 00:05:14,886
On this day,

88
00:05:14,936 --> 00:05:18,440
Akimoto Group chairman
holds a press conference.

89
00:05:19,200 --> 00:05:22,200
A ransom email from the
kidnappers has just arrived.

90
00:05:22,780 --> 00:05:26,360
It demands that we prepare one billion
yen in exchange for my daughter's life.

91
00:05:26,660 --> 00:05:28,140
One billion yen!?

92
00:05:28,560 --> 00:05:32,280
Compared to my precious Reiko's life,
it's a bargain.

93
00:05:32,760 --> 00:05:34,073
Calling a billion yen a bargain,

94
00:05:34,123 --> 00:05:37,020
that's just what you'd expect from
the chairman of the Akimoto Group.

95
00:05:37,640 --> 00:05:41,380
But we cannot let such a
heinous crime go unpunished.

96
00:05:42,340 --> 00:05:46,620
I, Penpenmaru Akimoto, have resolved
to bring my daughter Reiko back.

97
00:05:47,100 --> 00:05:47,460
What?

98
00:05:48,120 --> 00:05:53,360
We've always requested cooperation from
Germany's GSG9 and America's Green Berets.

99
00:05:53,820 --> 00:05:56,140
Colonel Kebel and the Bakuryu Team

100
00:05:56,760 --> 00:05:58,480
Chief, we can't just sit here!

101
00:05:58,480 --> 00:06:02,280
Let's reform the SS Team and head for Paris!

102
00:06:02,960 --> 00:06:04,940
The SS Team? That's already...

103
00:06:04,940 --> 00:06:07,060
If we don't do it, who will?

104
00:06:07,500 --> 00:06:11,920
If they rescue Reiko safely,
I'm prepared to pay 10 billion yen.

105
00:06:11,920 --> 00:06:14,860
10 billion?! Chief!

106
00:06:15,400 --> 00:06:18,320
We have to rescue Reiko no matter what.

107
00:06:20,060 --> 00:06:21,360
Ryotsu is on fire.

108
00:06:22,820 --> 00:06:25,340
I think I see something beyond the flames...

109
00:06:25,340 --> 00:06:28,420
Come on, Chief,
that's just your imagination.

110
00:06:28,420 --> 00:06:33,280
Never mind that, please hurry and
reform the SS Team and send me to Paris!

111
00:06:35,280 --> 00:06:37,800
I'll file a request with headquarters
through the station chief.

112
00:06:45,360 --> 00:06:47,300
On the honor of the Japanese police,

113
00:06:47,300 --> 00:06:50,980
make sure you bring
Officer Reiko Akimoto back.

114
00:06:50,980 --> 00:06:51,740
Understood.

115
00:06:51,740 --> 00:06:52,980
Bornosaigo,

116
00:06:53,480 --> 00:06:57,260
you've had experience shining in Glinvillet,
so I'm counting on you.

117
00:06:57,840 --> 00:06:58,820
Leave it to us.

118
00:06:59,360 --> 00:07:02,020
Sakonji, Honza, and Maria,
I'm counting on you too.

119
00:07:02,460 --> 00:07:02,800
Yes.

120
00:07:02,800 --> 00:07:21,240
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee!

121
00:07:21,240 --> 00:07:21,640
Hah!

122
00:07:21,920 --> 00:07:24,580
So I'm not expected to do anything at all?

123
00:07:27,180 --> 00:07:30,960
Hey, we're flying on a commercial plane?
And economy class?

124
00:07:31,720 --> 00:07:35,240
What's wrong? You look pale.

125
00:07:35,240 --> 00:07:37,960
I'm terrible with airplanes.

126
00:07:37,960 --> 00:07:41,260
Theory, protect me!

127
00:07:42,080 --> 00:07:44,200
Sir, is something wrong?

128
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:46,680
Don't stand behind me!

129
00:07:53,120 --> 00:07:53,740
Hey,

130
00:07:54,360 --> 00:07:56,720
Come on, quiet down.

131
00:07:56,720 --> 00:07:59,500
How am I supposed to
sleep with all this racket?

132
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:01,320
Bookshelf old man

133
00:08:02,100 --> 00:08:03,360
You there, Ryotsu!

134
00:08:03,360 --> 00:08:06,260
Father, what are you doing here?

135
00:08:06,260 --> 00:08:08,720
What are you two wearing?

136
00:08:08,720 --> 00:08:12,060
We're going to Paris to rescue Reiko,
who was kidnapped there.

137
00:08:12,060 --> 00:08:13,840
The same goes for me.

138
00:08:13,840 --> 00:08:15,200
Once we've rescued Reiko,

139
00:08:15,200 --> 00:08:18,680
we'll make the name of our Bookshelf
Prefecture resound across the whole world!

140
00:08:18,680 --> 00:08:19,600
Yeah.

141
00:08:19,600 --> 00:08:21,873
Saying "Huh?" or something like that,

142
00:08:21,923 --> 00:08:25,640
you're really after the 10 billion yen, aren't you?
You greedy pig!

143
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:29,700
What? You're the one after the money!

144
00:08:29,840 --> 00:08:31,820
No! I only want to save Reiko!

145
00:08:33,880 --> 00:08:36,720
See, you're after the
10 billion yen after all!

146
00:08:37,020 --> 00:08:39,900
Hey! What are you doing?

147
00:08:41,380 --> 00:08:42,180
That's it!

148
00:08:46,420 --> 00:08:47,740
Both of you, stop it!

149
00:08:49,760 --> 00:08:55,720
Hey, Economy Class General, what on
earth are you making such a fuss about?

150
00:08:56,800 --> 00:09:06,820
Ugh, Reiji Shiratori, another troublesome one!
Who'd have thought it was the super-poor Kankichi Ryotsu?

151
00:09:07,240 --> 00:09:11,540
Mind your own business! Who is this guy?

152
00:09:12,380 --> 00:09:13,420
Kankichi.

153
00:09:16,940 --> 00:09:17,320
What?

154
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:21,700
I'm surprised a Japanese
person doesn't know who I am.

155
00:09:21,700 --> 00:09:25,140
I'm Reiji Shiratori, the super-rich man.

156
00:09:25,140 --> 00:09:26,420
Remember that.

157
00:09:26,420 --> 00:09:31,900
Shiratori, you're not going to Paris too, are you?
Blinded by all that money?

158
00:09:31,900 --> 00:09:33,200
Tsk, tsk, tsk.

159
00:09:33,200 --> 00:09:37,760
A super-rich guy like me
has no interest in money.

160
00:09:37,760 --> 00:09:39,980
I have only one goal.

161
00:09:39,980 --> 00:09:46,780
To rescue Reiko, who will one day be my wife.
As usual, what a delusional bastard.

162
00:09:47,940 --> 00:09:53,180
Shiratori or whatever your name is, I'll rescue Reiko!
No, it's me!

163
00:09:54,300 --> 00:09:58,540
Don't be ridiculous!
The SS Team will rescue Reiko!

164
00:09:58,540 --> 00:10:26,080
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeh!

165
00:10:29,960 --> 00:10:33,260
Nakagawa's helicopter has
headed for Paris Nord station.

166
00:10:35,100 --> 00:10:36,640
I heard everything!

167
00:10:36,640 --> 00:10:38,440
Rush to Paris Nord station!

168
00:10:39,360 --> 00:10:40,800
Shut up!

169
00:10:47,920 --> 00:10:49,640
Hmph. That's the one.

170
00:10:50,120 --> 00:10:52,000
Alright, let's chase that helicopter!

171
00:11:29,960 --> 00:11:33,120
The curtains are closed,
so I can't see inside.

172
00:11:34,020 --> 00:11:34,560
Private car?

173
00:11:34,920 --> 00:11:37,460
No doubt about it!
Reiko is in the second car!

174
00:11:37,780 --> 00:11:39,900
The train is starting to move!

175
00:11:45,460 --> 00:11:46,880
Hey! Not again!

176
00:11:47,880 --> 00:11:49,240
Right, let's do it! It's impossible!

177
00:11:49,660 --> 00:11:52,920
A true imperial nation never gives up,
no matter what!

178
00:12:04,980 --> 00:12:06,320
Just as expected!

179
00:12:20,820 --> 00:12:22,500
According to the conductor's report,

180
00:12:22,500 --> 00:12:25,580
in this compartment of the second car,
in this position,

181
00:12:25,580 --> 00:12:27,800
a woman who looks like Miss Reiko is seated.

182
00:12:28,400 --> 00:12:31,773
The culprits are five in the combat car,
four in the second car,

183
00:12:31,823 --> 00:12:34,220
and eight have boarded the third car,

184
00:12:34,220 --> 00:12:36,600
each in the positions marked with an ×.

185
00:12:37,280 --> 00:12:40,400
The operation starts when
we enter the next tunnel.

186
00:12:40,400 --> 00:12:41,020
Understood.

187
00:12:48,400 --> 00:12:51,380
So the plan is to make our way
across the roof and take her back.

188
00:12:53,680 --> 00:12:55,100
Even her father...

189
00:12:55,100 --> 00:12:57,620
We're not letting those guys beat us to it.

190
00:12:58,260 --> 00:13:00,740
Nakagawa,
bring the helicopter closer to the train.

191
00:13:01,540 --> 00:13:03,580
You don't mean to jump across, do you?

192
00:13:03,580 --> 00:13:04,520
Of course.

193
00:13:04,880 --> 00:13:06,000
That's far too dangerous.

194
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:08,740
Don't you want to save Reiko Akimoto?

195
00:13:10,220 --> 00:13:10,860
Understood.

196
00:13:18,420 --> 00:13:19,160
Gyotz!

197
00:13:19,160 --> 00:13:21,960
Like I'd let them snatch the 10 billion yen!

198
00:13:22,600 --> 00:13:23,100
Come on!

199
00:13:25,840 --> 00:13:33,200
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

200
00:13:33,200 --> 00:13:34,920
Get off my back already!

201
00:13:36,100 --> 00:13:37,460
This is ridiculous.

202
00:13:40,240 --> 00:13:42,320
It would've been better
if he'd just fallen off.

203
00:13:42,900 --> 00:13:44,240
That guy's got nine lives.

204
00:13:44,240 --> 00:13:47,280
You can't kill me, I won't die!

205
00:13:49,360 --> 00:13:52,160
Four supercars all at once!

206
00:13:53,320 --> 00:13:55,040
Hey, poor man's shogun!

207
00:13:55,940 --> 00:13:57,360
Reiji Shiratori!

208
00:13:57,360 --> 00:13:59,280
How did you know about this train?

209
00:14:00,280 --> 00:14:03,200
I said I would rescue Reiko, didn't I?

210
00:14:03,200 --> 00:14:07,740
I spent my own pocket money
to hire some powerful helpers.

211
00:14:07,740 --> 00:14:08,720
Helpers.

212
00:14:08,720 --> 00:14:10,100
Well then, let me introduce them.

213
00:14:10,100 --> 00:14:12,860
Hey, I didn't ask you to introduce them!

214
00:14:13,380 --> 00:14:17,000
First, the former heavyweight
boxing champion, Mike.

215
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:19,260
What, Tyson?

216
00:14:19,260 --> 00:14:23,100
It's Mike Nisekovich,
who lives next door to Tyson.

217
00:14:24,120 --> 00:14:26,680
I figured it'd be something like this.

218
00:14:26,680 --> 00:14:29,840
There's more!
From K-1, I brought in this guy.

219
00:14:29,840 --> 00:14:33,560
Peter Aerts' second cousin, Andy Aerts.

220
00:14:33,560 --> 00:14:34,200
Hi there!

221
00:14:34,200 --> 00:14:38,000
I'm running out of energy to
even keep up with the jokes.

222
00:14:38,420 --> 00:14:40,500
And after K-1, it's F1!

223
00:14:40,880 --> 00:14:45,820
Michael Schumacher, the F1 giant,
who's driving my Porsche.

224
00:14:46,780 --> 00:14:48,540
This one really looks like the real thing.

225
00:14:48,540 --> 00:14:51,300
Michael Schumacher's lookalike,
Toad-Schumacher!

226
00:14:51,800 --> 00:14:52,520
Ribbit, ribbit.

227
00:14:55,020 --> 00:14:56,500
The last one is amazing!

228
00:14:56,500 --> 00:14:58,660
The Golgo everyone knows,

229
00:14:58,660 --> 00:14:59,980
Thirteen!

230
00:14:59,980 --> 00:15:02,160
It's Golgo Matsumoto.

231
00:15:02,700 --> 00:15:04,540
Hey, Mike! Hey, Mike!

232
00:15:04,540 --> 00:15:05,540
And Red Yushira, nice to meet you too.

233
00:15:05,540 --> 00:15:07,800
What are we doing hiring comedians?

234
00:15:08,380 --> 00:15:10,780
We're not like the amateurs from before!

235
00:15:10,780 --> 00:15:12,640
We're the real TIM.

236
00:15:12,640 --> 00:15:15,260
We were specially called in just for this.

237
00:15:15,260 --> 00:15:16,780
Let me get more involved!

238
00:15:17,460 --> 00:15:19,820
Well, good work on that.

239
00:15:19,820 --> 00:15:24,640
We're TIM! TIM! TIM! TIM!

240
00:15:24,760 --> 00:15:26,280
Shut up! Knock it off already!

241
00:15:26,440 --> 00:15:28,980
Their Golgo is a powerful helper!

242
00:15:29,140 --> 00:15:32,740
Renting supercars cost me all my money.

243
00:15:32,740 --> 00:15:35,240
Hah! You half-baked rich guy!

244
00:15:35,240 --> 00:15:38,760
Shut up! Anyway,
I'm the one who's going to save Reiko-san!

245
00:15:39,100 --> 00:15:41,080
Everyone, let's go along the roof!

246
00:15:43,560 --> 00:15:45,620
What is that guy?

247
00:15:47,420 --> 00:15:49,080
They're moving!

248
00:15:49,080 --> 00:15:50,520
It's a tunnel.

249
00:15:53,180 --> 00:15:55,120
Prepare to fire the second round!

250
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:02,120
Fire!

251
00:16:17,880 --> 00:16:18,820
What is it? What happened?

252
00:16:18,820 --> 00:16:20,280
They've broken through to the third car.

253
00:16:21,400 --> 00:16:21,760
Hey!

254
00:16:24,220 --> 00:16:26,660
Uncouple the second and third cars!

255
00:16:26,660 --> 00:16:27,360
Roger.

256
00:16:28,140 --> 00:16:28,700
Raid!

257
00:16:29,780 --> 00:16:31,500
Hey, let go!

258
00:16:33,120 --> 00:16:34,340
Let me help! I see, so that's how it is!

259
00:16:37,460 --> 00:16:39,880
Damn! They uncoupled it!

260
00:16:41,440 --> 00:16:42,900
Good grief!

261
00:16:44,720 --> 00:16:45,600
I won't let them get away!

262
00:16:51,260 --> 00:16:52,300
See ya!

263
00:16:58,580 --> 00:17:00,740
Idiot! What? Stop it!

264
00:17:01,060 --> 00:17:03,250
-Hey! Let go!

265
00:17:03,300 --> 00:17:05,540
We did it!-We did it!

266
00:17:05,880 --> 00:17:06,940
W-what?

267
00:17:09,740 --> 00:17:10,580
How about that?

268
00:17:11,180 --> 00:17:13,740
This should force the train to stop, right?

269
00:17:14,250 --> 00:17:16,200
Don't stop! Keep charging straight ahead!

270
00:17:16,360 --> 00:17:17,100
But!

271
00:17:17,260 --> 00:17:18,540
Just charge in!

272
00:17:20,740 --> 00:17:21,360
Hmph.

273
00:17:22,500 --> 00:17:23,420
How's that?

274
00:17:23,480 --> 00:17:24,500
Whoa!

275
00:17:27,860 --> 00:17:29,020
Aaaaaah!

276
00:17:29,020 --> 00:17:34,060
Supercars worth over 100
million yen are burning!

277
00:17:34,800 --> 00:17:35,820
Alright!

278
00:17:35,820 --> 00:17:36,620
See?

279
00:17:36,620 --> 00:17:38,280
Blazing!

280
00:17:39,580 --> 00:17:41,200
What an idiot.

281
00:17:42,980 --> 00:17:44,600
This music is...

282
00:17:47,380 --> 00:17:48,960
Colonel Bakley!

283
00:17:50,960 --> 00:17:54,800
Hahaha! Struggling against a bunch of kidnappers?
How pathetic!

284
00:17:54,800 --> 00:17:56,780
I'll lend you a hand.

285
00:17:56,780 --> 00:17:57,500
Damn it!

286
00:17:57,620 --> 00:17:59,220
Whoaaaaa!

287
00:17:59,420 --> 00:18:00,760
Noooooo!

288
00:18:01,240 --> 00:18:02,260
Aaaaaah!

289
00:18:05,280 --> 00:18:08,380
Hey! You went too far! Bakuryu Squad!

290
00:18:08,600 --> 00:18:12,060
Hahaha! I went easy on you, you know.

291
00:18:13,240 --> 00:18:15,240
Anyway, we've made an entry route.

292
00:18:17,420 --> 00:18:18,320
Reiko!

293
00:18:19,220 --> 00:18:20,140
Reiko!

294
00:18:25,440 --> 00:18:26,940
Damn, it's a dummy!

295
00:18:28,020 --> 00:18:28,600
What?

296
00:18:29,640 --> 00:18:56,620
Nooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooo! No, no, no, no, no, no, no, no,
no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no!

297
00:18:56,620 --> 00:18:59,960
Reiko! I'll definitely save your life!

298
00:19:00,720 --> 00:19:01,780
Ryo-chan...

299
00:19:01,780 --> 00:19:03,280
Sorry, but that's far enough!

300
00:19:03,860 --> 00:19:05,320
Transform!

301
00:19:09,220 --> 00:19:10,120
What!

302
00:19:11,300 --> 00:19:12,420
That's not fair!

303
00:19:13,680 --> 00:19:14,620
Farewell!

304
00:19:14,740 --> 00:19:15,640
Ryo-chan!

305
00:19:16,780 --> 00:19:17,400
Reiko!

306
00:19:20,320 --> 00:19:21,600
Ryo-chan!

307
00:19:26,720 --> 00:19:28,960
Wow, it's like we've walked
into a different show.

308
00:19:28,960 --> 00:19:32,120
That whole car belonged to the gang.

309
00:19:32,120 --> 00:19:33,340
Let's go after them.

310
00:19:33,340 --> 00:19:35,280
It's pointless, we can't possibly catch up.

311
00:19:35,280 --> 00:19:38,380
Hey, they're wrapping
something like paper around it.

312
00:19:39,460 --> 00:19:40,200
Damn it!

313
00:19:42,240 --> 00:19:43,260
What the hell is this?

314
00:19:43,820 --> 00:19:46,060
This isn't some damn sale announcement,
you idiot.

315
00:19:46,540 --> 00:19:50,080
If you want to save Reiko Akimoto,
come to Scotland.

316
00:19:50,080 --> 00:19:51,400
Mr. X

317
00:19:52,660 --> 00:19:55,580
Oh yeah? What's this Mr. X crap?
Don't screw with me!

318
00:19:55,800 --> 00:19:56,620
Pree!

319
00:20:00,240 --> 00:20:01,120
Ryo-chan!

320
00:20:03,780 --> 00:20:04,780
Hang in there, Reiko.

321
00:20:05,240 --> 00:20:08,900
Even if it costs me my life,
I'll get you out of there, no matter what.

